From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:54:59 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] libcutils: ashmem uapi header when built for Android

cutils/ashmem.h includes <linux/ashmem.h> under __BIONIC__ only,
while its callers (libandroid_runtime android_os_MemoryFile.cpp
ASHMEM_WAS_PURGED) use the ioctl definitions under __ANDROID__. A
device build against another C library defines __ANDROID__ but not
__BIONIC__; it then misses them. Widen the guard to
__BIONIC__ || __ANDROID__. No change for Soong variants: device
builds define both, linux_bionic defines __BIONIC__.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [no Soong variant defines __ANDROID__ without __BIONIC__]
Patch-Reason: the guard is compiled inside the libcutils header, out of reach of the launcher, loader and environment; defining __BIONIC__ instead would change the libc++ ABI on glibc
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 libcutils/include/cutils/ashmem.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libcutils/include/cutils/ashmem.h b/libcutils/include/cutils/ashmem.h
index 1913c1e4e716c046aa6e11e181c27215ae4850de..ccccd1465c794f35239b803129827e6a556d54c4 100644
--- a/libcutils/include/cutils/ashmem.h
+++ b/libcutils/include/cutils/ashmem.h
@@ -18,7 +18,7 @@
 
 #include <stddef.h>
 
-#if defined(__BIONIC__)
+#if defined(__BIONIC__) || defined(__ANDROID__)
 #include <linux/ashmem.h>
 #endif
 
